# Arduino Chess Clock ⏰♟️

A simple, fully functional chess clock for Arduino, built in C++ using **PlatformIO**.  
Supports classic time control and time increment.

## Features

- Configurable starting time (hours/minutes/seconds)
- Optional time increment (seconds and minutes)
- Visual feedback with Liquid Crystal  and LEDs 
- Audible signal (buzzer) on move switch and time expiration

## Hardware Requirements

- Arduino board (Mega2560 used in project)
- Push buttons end encoder
- Liquid Crystal screen LEDs 
- 1 buzzer (move sound + time warning)

All pins are defined in `include/pin_defines.h`


## Build & Upload (PlatformIO)

```bash
pio run              # Compile the project
pio run -t upload    # Upload to your Arduino
pio device monitor   # View serial output (debugging)